From 9b206209098f54c4f76553ea7b65a0270650c23f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:11:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/30] builds: delete a finished build from Recent builds

rdgen keeps its own copy of every build for RDGEN_RETENTION_DAYS, apart
from any copy a console imported, so deleting a client in the console
left rdgen's files (and the build in Recent builds) in place.

Delete on /builds (finished or failed builds, after a confirm) calls
poller.discard_build(): a conditional UPDATE sets deleted_at and
clears the manifest first, then the share links and the build directory
go. Terminal builds are never touched by the poller again, so nothing
writes the files back. Every lookup now skips deleted builds: the list,
check_for_file, /download, /share/*, /api/status, /api/download and
`rdgen_publish pending`. A hand-off that has not run is marked skipped;
one that is already running cannot undo the delete: `rdgen_publish
mark` leaves a deleted build alone and prints "deleted", so the job
can tell an expected failure from a real one. The row stays until
prune_local, so prune_remote still deletes a failed run on GitHub.
Copies already in the console stay there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
